    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n65237" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μάτη</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰ], ἡ</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>folly, fault</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μάτας
				εἰπών</span> speaking <i>folly</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Stesich.
				47
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ch.</u>
				918
			</span></i> (pl.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μάταισι πολυθρόοις</span>
			with clamorous <i>lewdness</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				820
			</span></i> (lyr.) (but expld. by Sch. as 'quest'); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὔ τί τοι μέτρον μάτας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					798
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μάτην</span> ad fin.</div>
